From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: do not hand back a secure assignment that failed

fastrpc_map_attach() set map->attr (FASTRPC_ATTR_SECUREMAP) before
qcom_scm_assign_mem(). When the assignment failed, the error path (since
0187: fastrpc_map_put() -> fastrpc_free_map()) saw SECUREMAP and tried to
assign the memory back from the DSP VM it never reached; that fails too,
and fastrpc_free_map() then returns early, leaking the map, its
attachment, mapping and dma-buf reference. Set the attribute only once
the assignment succeeded. Found by the GPT-6.1-Sol review of 0187.

Hardware: none on this phone's FastRPC users (no SECUREMAP maps).

diff --git a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
index a2f45baf7..39d7ef874 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -906,7 +906,6 @@ static int fastrpc_map_attach(struct fastrpc_user *fl, int fd,
 		dst_perms[0].perm = QCOM_SCM_PERM_RW;
 		dst_perms[1].vmid = fl->cctx->vmperms[0].vmid;
 		dst_perms[1].perm = QCOM_SCM_PERM_RWX;
-		map->attr = attr;
 		err = qcom_scm_assign_mem(map->dma_addr, (u64)map->len, &src_perms, dst_perms, 2);
 		if (err) {
 			dev_err(sess->dev,
@@ -914,6 +913,8 @@ static int fastrpc_map_attach(struct fastrpc_user *fl, int fd,
 				&map->dma_addr, map->len, err);
 			goto get_err;
 		}
+		/* Only an assigned map is handed back in fastrpc_free_map() */
+		map->attr = attr;
 	}
 	spin_lock(&fl->lock);
 	list_add_tail(&map->node, &fl->maps);
